        "y1": 0.5908680349639122
      },
      "text": "TROLL-MADAM. A game borrowed from the French in the 16th century, now known under the name of trunks, q. v. Brand quotes a curious account of this game, from which it appears to have formed a favorite indoor amusement with the lady fashionables at Buxton about the year 1572, and to have been somewhat like the modern game of bagatelle. There is an allusion to it in the Winter's Tale, iv. 2.",
